  [1mMy recommendation: stubbed behind a seam, unless you have the URLs handy.[0m The repo is a fixture with no network code
  and no test runner at all, so building against fakes is the only way to verify anything today. If the real contract
  differs later, what changes is the fake, not the design.

  One thing I'll fold into the design either way: this repo has [1mno tooling[0m — no linter, no formatter, no test runner, no
  dependencies in [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m. Adding async network calls and a tracking module without a way to test them means
  nothing here is verifiable. I'll propose setting up a minimal test runner as part of the spec, and you can cut it if
  you disagree.
